# Reversi: a board square 3 bytes (21 pixels) by 18 lines, empty, with each seat's disc, and with the
# mark of a legal move; the rv_s_ ones are 15 lines, for the 10 by 10 board. A Hi-Res pixel is about 7/6
# as tall as it is wide on a monitor, so 21 pixels by 18 lines is square there, and the discs are round: 14
# pixels (7 color pixels) by 12 lines in color (10 by 9 on 15 lines), 14 pixels by 12 lines in monochrome.
# Color squares come in two (both): a square at an odd byte column starts on an odd pixel. Made for this
# program.

color rv_empty both
.GGGGGGGGG
.GGGGGGGGG
.GGGGGGGGG
.GGGGGGGGG
.GGGGGGGGG
.GGGGGGGGG
